"## Flow: 9615\n\n- **Platform**: web\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/flows/9615\n- **Name**: Student Certificate Issuance\n- **Screens Count**: 6\n- **Description**: Happy path: an administrator/instructor navigates to a single student's Enrollments section, locates the course row, opens the row actions and chooses \"Issue Certificate\", selects a certificate from a modal, issues it, and sees confirmation and the new certificate entry in the Certificates table. Entry point: an admin is viewing a specific student's profile -> Enrollments tab. Exit point: Certificates table is updated and a toast confirmation appears. Assumptions: user is signed in with permission to manage enrollments/certificates, the student is already enrolled in the course shown, at least one certificate template exists for the course, and this is a desktop layout.\n- **Problem**: Task: manually issue a certificate to a student for a specific course. From the user's perspective: the admin wants to grant a certificate immediately (not wait for automatic criteria), so they find the student's enrollment, open the actions for that enrollment, pick a certificate template, and confirm issuance. Decisions: choose the correct course row, open the action menu, choose the \"Issue Certificate\" option, select the right certificate from the dropdown, and confirm. Expectations: immediate confirmation (toast) and a visible record in the Certificates section. From the system/interface perspective: the Enrollments table exposes an actions menu per course row with an \"Issue Certificate\" command that opens a modal with a certificate dropdown and Cancel / Issue controls; issuing creates a certificate entry associated with the student and course, displays a transient toast, and surfaces the certificate in the Certificates table with date and a Revoke action. End result: user-perceived outcome — a success toast and the issued certificate visible under Certificates (with date and Revoke option). System-level outcome — a certificate record is created/linked to the student and course and displayed in the UI (progress remains unchanged).\n\n### Site\n- **ID**: 358\n- **Name**:  Teachable\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/websites/358\n- **Domain**: teachable.com\n- **Categories**: Business\n- **Description**: Sell Courses, Coaching and Digital Downloads\n\n### Steps\n\n#### Step 1: View Enrollments\n- **Screen ID**: 0fd0afff-8d54-4deb-9148-cd6d277e298b\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/0fd0afff-8d54-4deb-9148-cd6d277e298b\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/teachable.com/desktop/fadf95f9-f6b5-410a-b8c0-9ebdb6d9d940_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: See which courses the student is enrolled in and check progress\n- **Action**: Admin reviews the Enrollments section for the selected student; locates the course row showing course name and progress (50%)\n- **System Response**: Displays Enrollments list with course rows, progress badges, and an actions (ellipsis) control for each row; Certificates section is visible lower on the page (empty initially)\n- **Page Types**: Content Management Page, Profile & Account\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Dropdown, Progress Bar, Sidebar & Drawer, Icon\n- **Fonts**: , San Francisco\n- **Content**\n  - Description: A modern enrollment management dashboard for an educational platform, showing a sidebar navigation, a manual course enrollment form, and a table of current enrollments with progress and actions.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with a dark left sidebar and a large white main panel; the main area stacks an enrollment form above an enrollments table with ample spacing and clear alignment.\n  - Functions: Users can choose a course to manually enroll, review existing enrollments and progress, and use an action menu for managing enrolled courses.\n\n#### Step 2: Open Course Actions\n- **Screen ID**: 657819bb-806e-4043-9008-b4fd476c5bba\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/657819bb-806e-4043-9008-b4fd476c5bba\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/teachable.com/desktop/0d169918-1bdf-4e41-b317-891f295bce62_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Access available management actions for that enrollment\n- **Action**: Admin clicks the actions (ellipsis) button on the course row\n- **System Response**: A contextual menu opens with options: Stats, Issue Certificate, Reset Course Progress, Unenroll\n- **UI Elements**: Action Sheet\n- **Fonts**: , San Francisco\n- **Content**\n  - Description: An admin-style enrollment management page for Liam's School showing a student profile sidebar, a manual course enrollment form, a table of current enrollments with progress, and an actions dropdown for course management.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with a fixed dark left sidebar and a scrollable main content area containing stacked cards for enrollment controls, a course table, and a small help/info box beneath.\n  - Functions: Allows selecting a course to enroll the student, reviewing existing enrollments and progress, and using per-course actions such as stats, issuing a certificate, resetting progress, or unenrolling; also includes a help link to documentation.\n\n#### Step 3: Launch Issue Certificate Modal\n- **Screen ID**: d5c7727b-ac44-4f60-8d2a-aa6c0ea9f8e6\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/d5c7727b-ac44-4f60-8d2a-aa6c0ea9f8e6\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/teachable.com/desktop/3ce58fc1-5ee3-454b-83c3-2ee035c64617_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Begin the manual certificate issuance process\n- **Action**: Admin selects \"Issue Certificate\" from the actions menu\n- **System Response**: A modal titled \"Issue Certificate\" opens with a certificate selection dropdown and Cancel / Issue buttons; the background page is dimmed\n- **UX Patterns**: Select\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Dropdown, Dialog & Modal Window, Popover\n- **Fonts**: , San Francisco\n- **Content**\n  - Description: An online education management dashboard titled \"Enrollments\" is shown with a centered \"Issue Certificate\" modal overlay. The modal includes a certificate dropdown, Cancel and bright yellow Issue buttons, while the dimmed page behind shows course enrollment controls and a progress table.\n  - Layout: Two-column admin layout with a dark fixed left sidebar and a main content area on the right. The main area has an \"Enrollments\" header, an enroll-in-course form, an enrollments table, and a centered modal dialog overlaid on top.\n  - Functions: The screen lets administrators enroll a student into a course, view enrollment progress, access row actions, and issue a certificate by selecting one from a dropdown in the modal. Cancel closes the dialog, and the Issue button confirms certificate issuance.\n\n#### Step 4: Select Certificate\n- **Screen ID**: a30d743f-f186-490c-8919-e04577cb5111\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/a30d743f-f186-490c-8919-e04577cb5111\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/teachable.com/desktop/96d841b9-603f-4e5d-8590-de7bb3b66cdd_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Choose the correct certificate template to issue\n- **Action**: Admin opens the certificate dropdown and selects the appropriate certificate entry (e.g., \"Certificate of Completion for Level Up: Fast-Track Your English...\")\n- **System Response**: Selected certificate text populates the dropdown within the modal; Issue and Cancel remain available\n- **UX Patterns**: Confirmation\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Dropdown, Dialog & Modal Window, Popover\n- **Fonts**: , San Francisco\n- **Content**\n  - Description: A course enrollment management page with a dark left sidebar, a main enrollments table, and a centered modal titled \"Issue Certificate\" overlaid on top.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with a vertical navigation sidebar on the left and the main content on the right; the modal is centered over the page with dropdown and action buttons.\n  - Functions: Users can select a course to enroll, view enrolled courses and progress, open an actions menu, and issue a certificate through the modal or cancel the action.\n\n#### Step 5: Confirm Issuance\n- **Screen ID**: 90968bb5-1220-4c71-9545-3ed014675a34\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/90968bb5-1220-4c71-9545-3ed014675a34\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/teachable.com/desktop/0bbe11d8-0847-4777-9d1e-32a656c25ee9_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Issue the selected certificate to the student\n- **Action**: Admin clicks the yellow Issue button in the modal\n- **System Response**: Modal closes and the system displays a transient toast/notification confirming the certificate has been issued (message shown at bottom of screen)\n- **UI Elements**: Notifications & Toast\n- **Fonts**: , San Francisco\n- **Content**\n  - Description: Minimal student enrollment management screen for John Doe, showing course enrollment controls, current enrollments, and a certificates area.\n  - Layout: Dark left sidebar with user info and navigation, plus a wide main column with stacked enrollment form, enrollments table, and partial certificates section.\n  - Functions: Lets admins choose a course to enroll the student, review enrollments with progress and actions, and manage certificates.\n\n#### Step 6: View Issued Certificate\n- **Screen ID**: 850c8c06-d949-4fa6-929e-b5d84f4867b6\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/850c8c06-d949-4fa6-929e-b5d84f4867b6\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/teachable.com/desktop/81c5c4cc-1491-4b1a-8284-e0128fa9634d_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Verify the certificate appears in the student's Certificates list\n- **Action**: Admin scrolls or views the Certificates section beneath Enrollments\n- **System Response**: Certificates table shows a new row with Course Name, Certificate title, Date Issued and a Revoke button; the issued certificate is now visible and can be revoked via the Revoke action\n- **Page Types**: Content Management Page, Profile & Account\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Dropdown, Progress Bar, Sidebar & Drawer, Icon\n- **Fonts**: , San Francisco\n- **Content**\n  - Description: A clean school admin dashboard for Liam's School showing the Enrollments page with a left navigation sidebar and management sections for enrolling a student, viewing enrolled courses and progress, and managing certificates.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with a dark vertical sidebar on the left and a white main content area on the right, where three stacked sections each pair explanatory text on the left with a card or table on the right.\n  - Functions: Allows admins to manually enroll a student in a course, review course enrollments and progress, open row actions, and revoke issued certificates.\n\n### Related Queries\n- manage student enrollments list\n- issue course certificate manually\n- manual reset course progress\n- revoke issued student certificate\n- enroll user in course manually\n- view student progress percentage\n- open enrollment actions menu\n- student certificates management list\n- select certificate and issue\n- admin issue certificate modal"
